        "original_id": "6addc646-c9ca-504b-8436-0601cab1b962",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Seven Seas to Calais\n- People: Rudolph Maté, Primo Zeglio, Sir Francis Drake\n- Roles: sea captain, privateer, vice admiral\n- Concepts: Elizabethan era\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Francis Drake was born around 1540 and died on 28 January 1596.\n- Sir Francis Drake was an English sea captain, privateer, and vice admiral of the Elizabethan era.\n- Seven Seas to Calais is a 1962 Italian adventure film made in Eastmancolor and CinemaScope.\n- Seven Seas to Calais was directed by Rudolph Maté and Primo Zeglio, and it was Rudolph Maté's final film.\n- Seven Seas to Calais depicts the career of Sir Francis Drake.",
